From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:59:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Draw themed save-state labels at the small text's own size

The save states' sheet sized its labels from the menu's small text,
whose size is already scaled by the screen's font scale, and the
grid's theme scaled it once more: on a 480 px high screen an 11 px
small text gave 14 px labels, and "start new autosave" ran past its
tile. With a theme's tiles (menuTile) the labels now take the small
text's own size; the stock tiles are unchanged.
---
 es-app/src/guis/GuiSaveState.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/es-app/src/guis/GuiSaveState.cpp b/es-app/src/guis/GuiSaveState.cpp
index ce5a8a27..26a41a12 100644
--- a/es-app/src/guis/GuiSaveState.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/guis/GuiSaveState.cpp
@@ -48,6 +48,12 @@ GuiSaveState::GuiSaveState(Window* window, FileData* game, const std::function<v
 	auto& tile = theme->Tile;
 	bool themedTiles = !tile.path.empty();
 
+	// The labels at the small text's own size: ES scales a theme's font size by the screen's font scale, and
+	// the small text's size is already scaled
+	float fontScale = Renderer::ScreenSettings::fontScale();
+	if (themedTiles && fontScale > 0.0f && fontScale != 1.0f)
+		sh = (std::ceil(theme->TextSmall.font->getSize() / fontScale) + 0.25f) / (float)Math::min(Renderer::getScreenHeight(), Renderer::getScreenWidth());
+
 	std::string gridSpacing = themedTiles ? "  <margin>8 0</margin>  <padding>4 6 4 6</padding>" : "  <margin>0.01 0.02</margin>  <padding>0 0</padding>";
 	std::string tileBackground = themedTiles ?
 		"  <backgroundImage>" + tile.path + "</backgroundImage>"
